From: SBE1V1K build <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommbe: 导出 QSDK dmac_* 缓存维护函数供 qca-nss-dp 使用

qca-nss-dp 的 ipq95xx EDMA 数据路径用 QSDK 的 dmac_inv_range()、
dmac_inv_range_no_dsb()、dmac_clean_range_no_dsb() 转移缓冲区所有权。
主线 6.12 只保留了改名后的 dcache_{inval,clean}_poc()，且都没有导出，
外部模块无法直接调用：

  exports/nss_dp_arch.h:182: error: implicit declaration of function
    'dmac_inv_range'; did you mean 'mas_find_range'?

本补丁在 arch/arm64/mm/flush.c 中恢复这三个函数并按 QSDK 的方式
EXPORT_SYMBOL。QSDK 的 *_no_dsb 汇编会省掉尾随 DSB；主线没有无屏障
原语，因此 *_no_dsb 包装改为调用常规 dcache_*_poc()（带 DSB），比
QSDK 更保守，这是唯一的行为差异。

dmac_flush_range()/dmac_clean_range() 未加入：使用者只有 ipq50xx 的
syn_gmac_dp，本目标不编译。

分类：必须 shim（厂商内核 ABI；主线原语存在但未导出）。
diff -ruN
--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/patches-6.12/0143-arm64-export-qcom-dmac-cache-helpers.patch	1970-01-01 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/patches-6.12/0143-arm64-export-qcom-dmac-cache-helpers.patch	2026-10-23 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,81 @@
+arm64: export the QSDK dmac_* cache maintenance helpers for qca-nss-dp
+
+qca-nss-dp's ipq95xx EDMA data path flushes buffer ownership with three
+QSDK cache helpers, declared in the vendor
+arch/arm64/include/asm/cacheflush.h and exported from
+arch/arm64/mm/flush.c:
+
+  dmac_inv_range()             -> dcache_inval_poc()
+  dmac_inv_range_no_dsb()      -> __dma_inv_area_no_dsb()
+  dmac_clean_range_no_dsb()    -> __dma_clean_area_no_dsb()
+  dmac_flush_range()           -> dcache_clean_inval_poc()
+
+Mainline 6.12 keeps the renamed primitives (dcache_inval_poc(),
+dcache_clean_poc(), dcache_clean_inval_poc()) but exports none of them,
+so an out-of-tree module cannot use them directly:
+
+  exports/nss_dp_arch.h:182: error: implicit declaration of function
+    'dmac_inv_range'; did you mean 'mas_find_range'?
+
+This patch restores the three helpers qca-nss-dp needs and exports them
+with EXPORT_SYMBOL like QSDK does.  The __dma_*_no_dsb assembly in QSDK
+skips the trailing DSB for speed; mainline has no barrier-free
+primitives, so the *_no_dsb wrappers call the regular dcache_*_poc()
+helper and carry their DSB.  That is strictly more conservative than
+QSDK and is the only observable difference.
+
+dmac_flush_range() and dmac_clean_range() are not added: their only users
+are the ipq50xx syn_gmac_dp files, which qca-nss-dp does not compile for
+this target.
+
+Classification: must-shim (vendor kernel ABI); mainline primitives exist
+but are not exported.
+
+diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/include/asm/cacheflush.h b/arch/arm64/include/asm/cacheflush.h
+--- a/arch/arm64/include/asm/cacheflush.h	2026-10-23 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
++++ b/arch/arm64/include/asm/cacheflush.h	2026-10-23 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+@@ -76,6 +76,13 @@
+ extern void dcache_clean_poc(unsigned long start, unsigned long end);
+ extern void dcache_clean_pop(unsigned long start, unsigned long end);
+ extern void dcache_clean_pou(unsigned long start, unsigned long end);
++/*
++ * QSDK compatibility: cache maintenance entry points used by qca-nss-dp's
++ * EDMA data path (see arch/arm64/mm/flush.c).
++ */
++extern void dmac_inv_range(const void *start, const void *end);
++extern void dmac_inv_range_no_dsb(const void *start, const void *end);
++extern void dmac_clean_range_no_dsb(const void *start, const void *end);
+ extern long caches_clean_inval_user_pou(unsigned long start, unsigned long end);
+ extern void sync_icache_aliases(unsigned long start, unsigned long end);
+ 
+diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/mm/flush.c b/arch/arm64/mm/flush.c
+--- a/arch/arm64/mm/flush.c	2026-10-23 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
++++ b/arch/arm64/mm/flush.c	2026-10-23 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+@@ -100,3 +100,27 @@
+ }
+ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(arch_invalidate_pmem);
+ #endif
++
++/*
++ * QSDK cache maintenance ABI.  qca-nss-dp hands buffer ownership to and
++ * from the EDMA engine with these calls.  The *_no_dsb variants exist in
++ * QSDK to skip the trailing DSB; mainline 6.12 has no barrier-free
++ * primitives, so they map to the standard dcache_*_poc() helpers.
++ */
++void dmac_inv_range(const void *start, const void *end)
++{
++	dcache_inval_poc((unsigned long)start, (unsigned long)end);
++}
++EXPORT_SYMBOL(dmac_inv_range);
++
++void dmac_inv_range_no_dsb(const void *start, const void *end)
++{
++	dcache_inval_poc((unsigned long)start, (unsigned long)end);
++}
++EXPORT_SYMBOL(dmac_inv_range_no_dsb);
++
++void dmac_clean_range_no_dsb(const void *start, const void *end)
++{
++	dcache_clean_poc((unsigned long)start, (unsigned long)end);
++}
++EXPORT_SYMBOL(dmac_clean_range_no_dsb);
